  "note": "Opens with the first composed Cuban guajira (Anckermann's El arroyo que murmura, 1899) and Joseíto Fernández's own Guantanamera, then the two faces of the genre at its radio-era height: punto proper (Indio Naborí's décimas and controversias, the improvised duels of Justo Vega and Adolfo Alfonso) and the guajira-son of Celina y Reutilio, Guillermo Portabales, Ramón Veloz and Coralia Fernández. Ends with EGREM-era Celina González and Albita and Radeúnda Lima. Many tracks come from later reissues, so their release year is left empty.",
